From: Catalyst Linux
Subject: [PATCH] cardputerzero-v5: the speaker plays both channels; the mic stays put

The AW8737A speaker amplifier takes the codec's left output only (LOUTP/N;
the right output goes to the headphone jack alone), so the speaker lost
the right channel of anything in stereo. Without headphones the right
channel is now mixed into the left, 6 dB down so the sum does not clip.

The jack no longer switches the microphone between the handheld's own
(MIC1) and a headset's (MIC2): headphones without a microphone left every
recording silent. catalyst-audio chooses it instead.

--- a/modules/CardputerZero/cardputerzero-v5-overlay.dts	2026-11-21 11:33:13.624395704 -0800
+++ b/modules/CardputerZero/cardputerzero-v5-overlay.dts	2026-11-21 11:35:58.857661281 -0800
@@ -389,12 +389,22 @@
 
                 simple-audio-card,hp-det-gpios = <&gpio 17 0>;
                 m5stack,hp-mute-pins = "Speaker";
+                /*
+                 * Catalyst Linux: the speaker's amplifier hangs off the
+                 * left output alone, so without headphones the right
+                 * channel is mixed into the left (6 dB down, so the sum
+                 * does not clip); headphones get both, as they are. The
+                 * microphone is not switched with the jack: headphones
+                 * without one would leave every recording silent.
+                 * catalyst-audio chooses it (the handheld's own unless
+                 * told otherwise).
+                 */
                 m5stack,hp-absent-controls =
-                    "PGAL Select=Line 1P",
-                    "PGAR Select=Line 1N";
+                    "IF DACL Mixer DACR DACL Mixer=on",
+                    "DACL Playback Volume=179";
                 m5stack,hp-present-controls =
-                    "PGAL Select=Line 2P",
-                    "PGAR Select=Line 2N";
+                    "IF DACL Mixer DACR DACL Mixer=off",
+                    "DACL Playback Volume=191";
 
                 simple-audio-card,aux-devs = <
                     &spk_mute_switch
